{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>בפקודיך אשיחה</b> — with my heart, that Your decrees are planted in it, and those who fulfill them will teach it to keep Your ways, which are straight in general principles, even though in particulars they may harm someone for whom the general principles are kept for good for all peoples. And the meaning of the matter you will understand from the rain, which is a general principle kept for good for the whole world, and in its generality, in that it benefits, there comes from it an evil occurrence for a few."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:14.782334952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}